! The spont_probe wiggler tracked by BMAD ITSELF: fel_method off so the FEL walk does
! not claim it, and tracking_method = runge_kutta so Bmad's integrator carries it
! through the same helical field, with Bmad's radiation damping applied from the
! element's own radiation integrals when the driver's radiation_damping knob is set.
! The independent reference for the spontaneous energy loss: no FEL model, no grid, no
! SVEA band.
!
! Both lines are needed. The FEL method and the tracking method are separate attributes,
! so setting the second no longer clears the first: an element is claimed by fel_method
! alone, and a lattice that wants Bmad's own tracking says so twice, once per axis.

call, file = spont_probe.bmad

UNDS[fel_method] = off
UNDS[tracking_method] = runge_kutta
UNDS[num_steps] = 400
